/ActualText (overly concerned about gaining weight. Taking in small, snacks every few hours throughout the day may help you avoid nausea. Try to stay away from strong odors, and spicy, greasy, or acidic foods. In rare cases, these measures are not effective and nausea and vomiting are severe. If you are not able to hold anything down for 24 hours, please call your obstetric provider. You could become dehydrated, which is not good for you or your baby. Your provider may prescribe medicine to help control vomiting, and may want you to visit the hospital for intravenous \(IV\) fluids to prevent dehydration.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [18]
>>
