>>
endobj
840 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (WHAT ABOUT TRAVELING?)
/E (WHAT ABOUT TRAVELING?)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
841 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In the beginning of your pregnancy, most traveling is okay. Try not to sit for long periods. Stretch your legs by taking a short walk at least every two hours, and keep your legs uncrossed in the car or plane. Later in your pregnancy \(after 28 weeks\), you should not travel without discussing it first with your obstetric provider.  Zika  Avoid traveling to areas with Zika virus. If travel is necessary, use insect repellent, wear long sleeves and pants, and stay in places with air conditioning or screened windows/doors. Consult your healthcare provider before traveling to Zika-affected areas. )
/E (In the beginning of your pregnancy, most traveling is okay. Try not to sit for long periods. Stretch your legs by taking a short walk at least every two hours, and keep your legs uncrossed in the car or plane. Later in your pregnancy \(after 28 weeks\), you should not travel without discussing it first with your obstetric provider.  Zika  Avoid traveling to areas with Zika virus. If travel is necessary, use insect repellent, wear long sleeves and pants, and stay in places with air conditioning or screened windows/doors. Consult your healthcare provider before traveling to Zika-affected areas. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
