858 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (CLEANING YOUR HANDS)
/E (CLEANING YOUR HANDS)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
859 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Practicing good hand hygiene is important any time, but especially when you are pregnant. Hand cleaning is the best way to prevent the spread of germs. Follow these steps, and ask others in your household to do the same.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
860 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (If using soap and water:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
861 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Wet hands first.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
862 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Apply soap.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
863 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Cover hands with soap; scrub for at least 15 seconds.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
864 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Rinse and dry thoroughly.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
865 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. Use paper towel to turn off faucet.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
866 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (If using waterless, alcohol-based hand cleanser:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
867 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Use only if hands are free of visible soil.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
868 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Pump cleanser into palm.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
869 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. Rub into all surfaces of your hands.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
870 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Continue rubbing until your hands are dry. No water )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
871 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (or paper towels are needed.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
872 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (MY PROVIDER HAS RECOMMENDED A TEST FOR HIV, THE VIRUS THAT CAUSES AIDS. WHY IS THIS IMPORTANT?)
/E (MY PROVIDER HAS RECOMMENDED A TEST FOR HIV, THE VIRUS THAT CAUSES AIDS. WHY IS THIS IMPORTANT?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
873 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
874 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The HIV virus can be passed on to the baby during pregnancy and birth, however, research has shown that if an individual who has the HIV virus takes certain medicines during pregnancy, the chance of passing the virus to the baby is greatly decreased. This is why the HIV test is now recommended for pregnant individuals.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
875 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (MAY I GO TO THE DENTIST?)
/E (MAY I GO TO THE DENTIST?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
876 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (It is safe to continue routine dental care during pregnancy. In fact, there is a good reason to make sure you have at least one visit to the dentist during your pregnancy. Hormones can cause a more resistant form of plaque to develop on your teeth. You may be more prone than usual to cavities and gum disease.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
877 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (It is okay to have Novacaine if you need it for a filling or another reason. Even dental x-rays are alright during pregnancy as long as you wear a lead shield on your abdomen. If you have been advised to take antibiotics before any dental work, you should continue this practice during pregnancy as well.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
878 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (WHAT ABOUT SMOKING, ALCOHOL, OR OTHER DRUGS?)
/E (WHAT ABOUT SMOKING, ALCOHOL, OR OTHER DRUGS?)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
879 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (All of these things must be stopped while you are pregnant. Smoking has been clearly shown to cause lower birthweight babies, and is associated with an increased risk of miscarriage, pregnancy complications, and sudden infant death syndrome \(SIDS\).)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
880 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText <>
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
881 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Cannabis \(also known as Marijuana\) use in pregnancy has been associated with a higher risk of childhood mental health issues like Autism and ADHD. Please abstain from using Cannabis during pregnancy.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
882 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (14)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
883 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Recreational drugs are harmful to you as well as your baby and must not be used during pregnancy. Babies born to mothers who have used drugs can have serious health problems, including drug addiction.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
884 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (If you have any questions or need help to stop using )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
885 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (these substances, please be sure to talk with your )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
886 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (obstetric provider. Many face this challenge during )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
887 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (pregnancy, and your providers can advise you on )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
888 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (getting the help you need.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
889 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Toxoplasmosis)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [41]
>>
endobj
