942 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Many immunizations or vaccinations given to prevent disease are okay to have during pregnancy; however, a few are not safe. The rubella vaccine \(German measles\) and the varicella vaccine \(chickenpox\) are not given during pregnancy. Rubella is often given as an MMR vaccine, which combines rubella with the measles and mumps vaccination. Talk with your obstetric provider about any immunization shots you may be having because of travel or routine care.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
943 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Pregnant individuals are more prone to complications )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
944 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (from the flu. Flu vaccines are recommended for all )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
945 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (those who are pregnant. Talk with your provider about )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
946 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (when you should receive a flu shot. A TDAP booster is )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
947 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (recommended in the third trimester to help protect the )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
948 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (baby from pertussis \(whooping cough\).)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
949 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The COVID-19 vaccine is also recommended during pregnancy to protect both mother and baby. Additionally, the recently approved RSV vaccine can help protect newborns from respiratory syncytial virus. Consult your healthcare provider for timing and options for these vaccines.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
