/T (In pregnancy, we refer to time in weeks, not months. The average pregnancy lasts about 40 weeks from your last menstrual period \(LMP\). We label each week once it is completed; for example, you will be "24 weeks" when you finish the 24th week. This approach provides a more precise timeline for monitoring pregnancy and development milestones.)
